msgctxt "Addon Summary"
msgid "Forces software decoding for video that hardware decoding gets wrong - by path, by series or on demand - then restores hardware decoding."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "Addon Description"
msgid "CoreELEC's amcodec hardware decoder mishandles some videos: rotated phone/camera clips usually play stretched, some old MJPEG AVI clips won't play at all, and some 50 fps video drops frames. Limp forces software decoding just for the videos that need it, then restores hardware decoding. Apply it to files under paths you choose (or everywhere), to TV series you pick, or to any single video from the context menu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32000"
msgid "By Path"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32014"
msgid "Apply everywhere (not recommended!)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32015"
msgid "Applies to every video played, not just under the paths below. Not recommended - without a path to exclude modern high-resolution video, this can force unnecessary, CPU-heavy software decoding on files that don't need it."
msgstr ""

